# How to read this file
#   ##  lines are notes. Leave them as they are.
#   KEY=value          is on. Copy it as is.
#   # KEY=value        is optional and off. Delete the "# " to turn it on.
#
# Copy to apps/mobile/.env for local dev. Every variable here is optional. EAS
# builds take their values from the build profile in eas.json (and EAS
# environment variables), not from this file.
#
# Every EXPO_PUBLIC_ value is baked into the bundle: restart Metro with a clean
# cache (`npx expo start -c`) after changing one, and never put a secret here.
#
# The phone app doesn't use NODE_ENV. Its equivalent is React Native's __DEV__,
# true only in a development build served by Metro (docs/environments.md).


# ==============================================================================
# Where the API and Storage are
# ==============================================================================
## A phone is not your laptop: `localhost` resolves to the phone itself. Leave
## these two off and a development build uses the address Metro is served from,
## so it follows you between networks. `npm run mobile:tunnel` sets them to its
## tunnel URLs. A preview or production build must have both, or it throws at
## launch.

# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.10:3001

## Only used to rewrite signed file links so a phone can reach local Storage.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://192.168.1.10:54321


# ==============================================================================
# Environment and error reporting (docs/error-handling.md)
# ==============================================================================

## [optional] development | staging | production. Only tags Sentry reports. EAS
## builds set it per profile in eas.json (development, preview → staging,
## production); leave it off for local dev.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development

## [optional] Sentry DSN. Off = no error reporting. Needs a build made after
## the @sentry/react-native plugin was added (Oct 2026).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=


# ==============================================================================
# Subscriptions (docs/billing.md)
# ==============================================================================
## [optional] RevenueCat public SDK keys, one per platform. Off hides buying.
## Until the stores are connected, a RevenueCat Test Store key (test_...) in
## both works on either platform. Needs a development build made after
## react-native-purchases was added (Oct 2026).

# EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY=

# EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_KEY=


# ==============================================================================
# Google sign-in (docs/sign-in.md)
# ==============================================================================
## OAuth client IDs from Google Cloud. Off hides the Google button. Sign in with
## Apple needs nothing here. Both need a dev build made after they were added
## (Nov 2026).

## The Web client ID. Android needs it to get an ID token.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=<web>.apps.googleusercontent.com

## The iOS client ID. app.config.js also turns it into the URL scheme Google's
## sheet returns to.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=<ios>.apps.googleusercontent.com
